---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_UPDATED } from '../data/site';
const updated = new Date(LEGAL_UPDATED).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' });
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy Policy – PDFNU" description="PDFNU processes your files locally in your browser and never uploads them. Read how we handle cookies, Google AdSense, consent and your rights." h1="Privacy Policy" path="/privacy"
  lead={`Last updated: ${updated}. The short version: your files never leave your device. The site itself uses a few cookies for ads, with your consent where the law requires it.`}>
  <h2>1. Your files</h2>
  <p>
    Every PDFNU tool processes files <strong>locally in your web browser</strong> using JavaScript and WebAssembly. The files you select, their contents,
    their names and the results are <strong>never uploaded</strong> to PDFNU or to anyone else, and we have no ability to see them. They exist only in your
    browser’s memory while the page is open and in the downloads you choose to save. Passwords you type into Protect PDF are also processed only on your device.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information we don’t collect</h2>
  <p>PDFNU has no accounts, no sign-up and no analytics or tracking scripts of our own. We don’t sell personal data.</p>

  <h2>3. Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    The website is served by Cloudflare. When your browser requests a page, Cloudflare processes technical data such as your IP address, browser
    type and requested URL to deliver the page and protect the site against abuse. This data doesn’t include your files. See
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Storage on your device</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Theme preference:</strong> if you switch between light and dark mode, the choice is saved in your browser’s local storage.</li>
    <li><strong>Offline cache:</strong> a service worker stores the site’s pages, code and processing engines on your device so the tools load quickly and work offline. It never stores your files.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can clear both at any time by clearing site data in your browser settings.</p>

  <h2>5. Advertising (Google AdSense)</h2>
  <p>
    PDFNU is funded by ads served by Google AdSense. Google and its partners may use cookies and similar technologies to show ads, limit how often you see them,
    measure performance and, with your consent where required, personalise ads based on your visits to this and other websites.
    Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>EEA, UK and Switzerland:</strong> before any non-essential cookies are used, a consent message from Google’s certified consent management platform lets you accept, reject or customise. Until you choose, ads run in a limited, non-personalised mode.</li>
    <li><strong>Change your choice:</strong> use the “Privacy choices” link in the footer (shown where available) or clear this site’s cookies.</li>
    <li><strong>Opt out of personalised ads:</strong> visit <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Ads never have access to the files you process.</p>

  <h2>6. Legal bases (GDPR / UK GDPR)</h2>
  <p>
    Delivering the website and protecting it from abuse relies on our legitimate interest. Advertising cookies and personalised ads rely on your consent,
    which you can withdraw at any time. Because we don’t receive your files, they aren’t processed by us under any legal basis.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete or object to the processing of personal data, and to complain to your
    data protection authority. As we hold almost no personal data, most requests concern advertising cookies, which you control through the consent
    choices above. For anything else, contact us.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Children</h2>
  <p>PDFNU isn’t directed at children under 13 (or the minimum age in your country) and doesn’t knowingly collect their personal data.</p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>We’ll update this page if our practices change, and revise the date at the top.</p>

  <h2>10. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
